commit 826d50ff78f83b4d55ce46afd3d1dd5735d18898
Author: Martin Oberzalek <martin.oberzalek@anton-paar.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 23 13:25:55 2026 +0200

    move vendored miniLZO out of the cpputils submodule
    
    cpputils is a git submodule, so writing our dependency inside it would dirty the
    submodule, place our code in someone else's tree, and could not be committed from
    this repository. miniLZO will be vendored into third_party/minilzo/ instead.
    
    Updates PLAN_rfa_tools.md (deliverable layout, Phase 1.4, decision D4 and its
    consequences) and the AGENTS.md conventions.

commit 7de64325266b21c17d304753bab1dbe076b1ff22
Author: Martin Oberzalek <martin.oberzalek@anton-paar.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 23 13:23:41 2026 +0200

    Phase 0 done: oracle harness, golden CLI capture, corrected format model
    
    Implements Phase 0 of PLAN_rfa_tools.md and records what running its exit gate
    turned up.
    
    * bin/*.orig.exe: immutable oracle backups, SHA-256 verified against both the
      repo copies and the bf_pablov_mod copies.
    * tools/rfa_probe.py: container dumper and structural validator.
    * tools/rfa_names.py: stable sorted TSV directory dump, for diffing.
    * tools/rfa_oracle.py: drives the originals, captures rc/stdout/stderr and
      snapshots extracted trees with sizes and SHA-256.
    * tools/rfa_golden.py + tests/golden/oracle-cli.json: 11 captured CLI scenarios
      (usage banners, the terse error strings, exit codes) with a --check mode.
    
    Format model corrected after sweeping every .rfa in bf_pablov_mod (814 archives,
    448127 entries, 99.99% structurally consistent):
    
      - the block header's first field is a chunk count, not a constant tag == 1,
        and the descriptor table grows 12 bytes per extra chunk
      - payloads are compressed per 32 KiB chunk, not per file
      - storedSize == uncompressedSize means a raw payload with NO block header
        (34617 entries, including 235 inside version-1 archives)
      - version is 0 or 1 and does not select the payload layout
      - uncompressedSize == 0 entries have storedSize == 4
    
    The constant-tag error is invisible on single-chunk files, which is exactly what
    the small fixtures are; it survived the original probe matrix and two doc reviews.
    
    Also records that the originals' exit codes are not a success signal (-i9999 and
    the broken -f both exit 0) and that line order in their stdout is unstable under
    redirection, both of which constrain the Phase 3 compatibility tests.
    
    Updated rfa-format.md, AGENTS.md, tests/data/README.md and PLAN_rfa_tools.md.
    Phase 0 exit gate passes: all four fixtures validate with exit 0 and zero
    problems, and rfa_golden.py --check reproduces.

commit 531269b150cd98e879a58a6fd2e19ba7e575b4da
Author: Martin Oberzalek <martin.oberzalek@anton-paar.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 23 13:13:48 2026 +0200

    added RFA tooling skills, oracle binaries and test data
    
    Preparing the rfaPack/rfaUnpack reimplementation (see PLAN_rfa_tools.md).
    
    * .github/skills: copied the RFA-relevant skills from bf_pablov_mod
      (rfa-unpack, bf1942-standalone-map) and corrected the format docs:
      payload compression is LZO1X, entry nameLen has no NUL terminator,
      and the entry flags field is per-entry rather than an archive constant.
    * bin: original vendor rfaPack.exe/rfaUnpack.exe kept as the test oracle.
    * tests/data: four real .rfa fixtures (one 251-entry FH map plus three tiny
      archives covering the stored and LZO1X paths) with SHA-256 provenance.
    * AGENTS.md: build instructions and the verified format facts.
    * .vscode: cygwin make build tasks.
    * .gitignore: ignore *.o and the future /bin/new/ shadow deploy dir.

